WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.103
A cookie holding only an

00:00:01.903 --> 00:00:03.677
empty pair of braces can

00:00:03.477 --> 00:00:05.487
log attackers into your Xen

00:00:05.287 --> 00:00:06.746
Orchestra console.

00:00:07.446 --> 00:00:09.241
CISA listed it as exploited

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.905
on November twenty-fifth,

00:00:10.705 --> 00:00:11.875
with nine others.

00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:13.503
Most are due by Saturday,

00:00:13.303 --> 00:00:14.952
right through Thanksgiving.

00:00:15.502 --> 00:00:17.346
The server turns that cookie

00:00:17.146 --> 00:00:19.059
into an empty database filter.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:21.354
It matches every stored token,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.041
so the attacker can inherit

00:00:22.841 --> 00:00:24.508
the first stored one and

00:00:24.308 --> 00:00:25.829
pull reusable logins.

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:28.378
Vates warned on November tenth

00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:30.454
that it was already being exploited.

00:00:30.494 --> 00:00:31.755
The CVE number,

00:00:31.555 --> 00:00:33.311
rated nine point eight,

00:00:33.111 --> 00:00:35.009
only came on the twenty-third.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:36.943
The fix is six point

00:00:36.743 --> 00:00:38.054
nine point two,

00:00:37.854 --> 00:00:39.608
or six point ten point one.

00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:41.041
But a second flaw let

00:00:40.841 --> 00:00:42.630
the attacker reach the hosts

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.154
underneath, and it had no

00:00:43.954 --> 00:00:45.147
fix at last update.

00:00:45.697 --> 00:00:47.570
Strip VM import rights where

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.685
they are not needed.

00:00:48.725 --> 00:00:50.148
Keep the console on a

00:00:49.948 --> 00:00:51.303
management network.

00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:52.642
Then hunt for a VM

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:53.595
named pivot two.

00:00:54.145 --> 00:00:55.750
Juniper also has a bug

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.451
that lets attackers with no

00:00:57.251 --> 00:00:59.743
credentials run commands as root,

00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:00.778
fixed in October.

00:01:00.818 --> 00:01:02.529
Mitel has five flaws that

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:03.321
need no login.

00:01:03.871 --> 00:01:05.282
Three of the ten live

00:01:05.082 --> 00:01:07.705
in software that manages other machines.

00:01:07.745 --> 00:01:09.152
Own one, and you own

00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:10.426
everything it manages.

00:01:10.466 --> 00:01:12.933
Take consoles off the open internet.

00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:15.426
Every fixed version and trace

00:01:15.226 --> 00:01:16.332
to hunt for is in

00:01:16.132 --> 00:01:17.169
the full story.

